docs/shots-motion/

# Selcom wire captures — contain the Authorization header (base64 API key).
# Evidence for a support ticket, never for git history.
selcom-capture-*.txt
selcom-email-*.md

# Database backups (npm run db:backup). NEVER committed: even sealed, these are a
# complete copy of every player balance, phone number, NIDA and KYC record on the
# platform. They belong in the encrypted CI artifact / R2 bucket, not in git.
backups/

# The disposable Postgres cluster npm run db:scratch boots for db:verify-backup.
# During a verification run it holds a FULLY RESTORED copy of the money database —
# every balance, phone number, NIDA and KYC record — in plaintext on disk.
.pgscratch/

# QA screenshot output (regenerated by qa:cert-c1 / qa:cert-c3)
.qa-shots/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Live-QA run artifacts — screenshots, shadow samples, build logs. Evidence, not source.
.qa-artifacts/

# ⭐ REGENERABLE SCREENSHOTS. A driver writes these on every run, so committing them grows the
# repo without adding a fact — `shots/` reached 32 MB of which 8 MB was the same few pages shot
# over and over. Anything a script can recreate on demand is ignored here; a screenshot that is
# EVIDENCE for a finding is committed under its own `shots/<FINDING>/` directory and is cited by
# `docs/`, which `npm run test:docs` now checks actually exists.
shots/chrome/
shots/emails/
shots/*.png

# Live-QA session scratch — probe logs, ad-hoc shots, RED/GREEN transcripts. The EVIDENCE
# lives in docs/LIVE-QA-CAMPAIGN.md; these are the raw files it was read from and they are
# regenerated by the scripts in scripts/, so committing them only grows the repo.
.qa-s2*/
.qa-s2*.txt
.qa-s2*.log
/s2?-*.png
# ⚠️ `.qa-s2*` does NOT cover session 30. The pattern was written when the session number
# happened to start with a 2, and the next session's scratch would have been committed
# silently. Widened rather than renamed, so session 29's paths in the campaign doc still hold.
.qa-s3*/
.qa-s3*.txt
.qa-s3*.log
/s3?-*.png
# 🔴 THE LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING (2026-08-08, session 37). Unanchored, `s2?-*.png`
# matches at ANY depth — so it silently claimed `shots/S27/s27-add-chain.png`, which is
# COMMITTED EVIDENCE cited by LIVE-QA-CAMPAIGN §E-89 and checked by `npm run test:docs`.
# A cleanup that trusted `git ls-files -i` would have deleted a finding's only proof.
# These patterns mean "session scratch dropped in the repo ROOT", so they say so.

# Design-brief build output — regenerate with `node scripts/build-design-brief.mjs`.
# The AUTHORED parts are versioned in docs/design-brief/; this is the assembled package.
/design-brief/
/design-brief.zip

# The identity pack is zipped for handoff; the folder beside it is the source.
docs/design-brief/*.zip
design-brief-ALL.txt
design-brief-lite/
